    {
      "name": "StartHere",
      "type": "comment",
      "parameters": {},
      "seed_int": 0,
      "node_position": {
        "x": -650,
        "y": -750
      },
      "title": "Copy, author, export, reload",
      "size": {
        "x": 1550,
        "y": 200
      },
      "color": {
        "type": "Color",
        "r": 0.18,
        "g": 0.23,
        "b": 0.28,
        "a": 1
      },
      "text": "Copy this file to terrain/surfaces/my_material/my_material.ptex. Edit AuthorControls: stone colors, grain scale, repeat metres, relief metres, normal strength and roughness. Select Material for the real PBR color/normal/roughness preview. AO is 1; add cavity occlusion when the surface needs it. Save, run tools/materials/export.py, then RELOAD ASSETS. Assign a new material name to a game consumer first. The official CLI texture route exports 2048 square images. Packed game outputs are color+height, normal+AO, roughness and physical metadata. No source bitmap or Buffer is used."
    }
